# Each long-running service writes <YYYYMMDD>-<service>.log here (QTE_LOG_DIR),
# and docker-compose mounts this directory into them. Tracked so the directory
# exists before the first `up`: a bind mount of a missing directory is created
# by the Docker daemon, and on a Linux host that leaves it root-owned.
#
# Being tracked is not enough to make it writable, though. A clone belongs to
# whoever ran it, while the containers run as uid 10001 (`USER qte` in the
# Dockerfile), so on a Linux host nothing here is writable by the services
# until someone hands that uid the directory — which is what `make
# log-directory` does, as a prerequisite of every target that starts the stack.
# Without it the services still run, logging to the console alone.
#
# The .log files themselves are git-ignored.
